{
  "schemaVersion": "0.1.0",
  "status": "P00-review-draft",
  "rules": [
    "Connectivity is a separate observation; link loss never releases a reservation.",
    "Guard names specify required evidence; declaring a guard true is not production proof or authorization.",
    "No provider, Jev result or delivery acknowledgment accepts a task.",
    "No unspecified transition is allowed; clients cannot select a from-state without the owner current revision.",
    "Every transition also requires an authenticated actor bound to the owner scope and a conditional commit against the current entity revision. Actor role strings supplied by a client never prove this authority.",
    "Kernel resource classes are reserved. Ordinary capability requests may only subscribe to kernel-status. Broker permissions and the protected assembly must enforce this independently of manifest validation.",
    "Private children receive newly scoped service handles and grants bound to the exact parent grant revision. Independent references retain independent lifecycle and authority.",
    "Cancellation remains recorded through unknown outcomes. Resuming an uncertain attempt requires proof that no cancellation remains pending."
  ],
